# FODIP Digital 2030 - Trivy image-scan exceptions (Sprint Enterprise 0, Lot 1).
#
# Every entry below was reviewed individually against the real scan output (PR #38), not
# batch-suppressed: for all 14, Trivy itself reports an EMPTY "Fixed Version" - no patched Debian
# bookworm package exists yet for any of them, several explicitly marked will_not_fix/fix_deferred
# by Debian's own security team. None come from this repository's own code or dependencies (see
# docs/19-GOUVERNANCE-SUPPLY-CHAIN.md for how that was confirmed for the two findings that briefly
# looked like they might be) - all fourteen are base-image-only (node:22-bookworm-slim's OS
# packages: util-linux, perl, zlib, systemd, ncurses, gzip, acl).
#
# Re-review this file whenever `docker compose build` picks up a newer node:22-bookworm-slim
# build (Dependabot tracks the base image, per .github/dependabot.yml): a line here whose fix
# has since shipped upstream should be removed, not left stale. Never add an entry here for a
# finding that has a real fix available - only for a genuinely unfixable base-image CVE.

# util-linux (bsdutils, libblkid1, libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount, util-linux,
# util-linux-extra) - TOCTOU via ancestor directory swap during mount. Debian status: affected,
# no fixed version. This image's runtime user (`node`, non-root) never invokes `mount`.
CVE-2026-53613

# gzip - information disclosure via global buffer overflow in LZH decompression. Debian status:
# fix_deferred, no fixed version. gzip is never invoked by this image at runtime.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 - symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl functions. Debian status: affected
# (implicit), no fixed version. Not linked against by anything this image runs.
CVE-2026-54369

# systemd (libsystemd0, libudev1) - local privilege escalation via systemd-homed missing
# home-record signature verification. Debian status: affected, no fixed version. systemd-homed
# is not present or reachable in this container (no init system, no user home records).
CVE-2026-16742

# ncurses (libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) - buffer overflow, potential arbitrary code
# execution. Debian status: affected, no fixed version. Not invoked by this image (no interactive
# terminal UI in either the API or the Next.js server).
CVE-2025-69720

# perl-base - incorrect regular expression processing via large regular expressions. CRITICAL.
# Debian status: affected, no fixed version. Perl is bundled with the base image but never
# invoked by either application at runtime (Node.js only).
CVE-2026-13221

# perl-Archive-Tar - path traversal via crafted symlinks. Debian status: fix_deferred, no fixed
# version. Same reasoning as CVE-2026-13221: perl-Archive-Tar is never invoked here.
CVE-2026-42496

# perl - heap buffer overflow when compiling regular expressions, 32-bit builds only. This image
# is amd64/x86_64 (docker-compose.yml, CI runners) - the vulnerable code path does not apply here
# regardless of Debian's fix status, but perl is unused either way (see CVE-2026-13221).
CVE-2026-8376

# perl-Archive-Tar - arbitrary file modification via crafted hardlinks during archive extraction.
# HIGH. Debian status: fix_deferred, no fixed version. perl-Archive-Tar never invoked here.
CVE-2026-42497

# perl-IO-Compress - arbitrary code execution via attacker-controlled output glob. Debian status:
# affected, no fixed version. perl-IO-Compress never invoked here.
CVE-2026-48962

# perl - information disclosure via integer overflow in pack/unpack. Debian status: affected, no
# fixed version. Perl never invoked here.
CVE-2026-57432

# Storable (bundled with perl) - denial of service via signed integer overflow in
# deserialization. Debian status: affected, no fixed version. Never invoked here.
CVE-2026-57433

# perl-Archive-Tar - denial of service via crafted tar header with an oversized entry. Debian
# status: fix_deferred, no fixed version. perl-Archive-Tar never invoked here.
CVE-2026-9538

# zlib1g - integer overflow and heap-based buffer overflow in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6. CRITICAL.
# Debian status: will_not_fix (Debian's own security team has explicitly declined to patch this
# one, not merely "not yet"). zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6 is a zlib zip-writing helper neither Node.js
# nor either application here calls (Node's own zlib usage is read/decompress-oriented; no zip
# file is ever created by this codebase).
CVE-2023-45853
